{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030587-how-the-traditions-incorporate-computers-and-the-internet","id":1030587,"title":"How the Traditions Incorporate Computers and the Internet","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-12T07:54:43-08:00","id":1030587,"title":"How the Traditions Incorporate Computers and the Internet","content":"The internet has basically become a necessity for modern living these days. In most developed countries, it's become the main way, and in some cases the only way, to seek opportunities, keep records, hold meetings and discussions, and learn about things we aren't able to experience directly.<br /> <br /> It could be argued that a lot of mages would shy away from computers and the internet because of how much influence the Technocracy has over this stuff. But in the same way that cars, guns, lights, and such have become commonplace in a number of earthbound practices. I'd think that by now computers would be as part of the fabric of their practices as the rest of it.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that these traditions are using computers and the internet as the primary method of doing magic. That's always been a VA thing. But I'm wondering how people think the traditions, and the crafts for that matter, would start to adopt this tech into their everyday practices.<br /> <br /> For example. I can quite easily imagine a number of Hermetics incorporating CD and DVD libraries into their traditional libraries. Sure nothing really beats a good tome, but if you need to transmit the written word in a hurry, these machines can be pretty useful. I can also picture a number of tech savvy Hermetics booby-trapping their desktops with passwords that create magical effects if typed slightly incorrectly.<br /> For the Verbena, I'd imagine they'd be much more resistant to the idea. Moonseekers might be more accepting of it than others though. Perhaps blogging is one Witch's primary method of teaching her lessons and keeping their legends alive. Maybe they even use Excel to keep tabs on their herb inventory.<br /> Etherites would be a mixed bag here. I can imagine a number of them using computers like anyone else would, but I can also imagine them hearkening back to the days of analogue machines, where if you can't literally see its parts working, it probably isn't very well made.<br /> <br /> How do you imagine mages incorporating computers and the internet into their general practices?<br /> <br /> (Also, can I request that we leave the Virtual Adepts out of this? We know that Computers and the Internet have been their thing since before it was cool. I'm not sure what more could be said about their relationship with Computers.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T12:13:43-08:00","id":1030717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not saying that these traditions are using computers and the internet as the primary method of doing magic. </div> </div> </div>Well, they ARE doing it. In each and every Tradition there's at least a small group of Technomancers, and many of them use the Internet as an integral part of their magick.<br /> <br /> Technoshamans are big on this because the Digital Web it's heavily related to the Middle Umbral counterpart of the internet (don't remeber the name).<br /> Also, House Verditus has been know to create magical computers.<br /> <br /> But every Tradition (perhaps with the exeption of the Verbena) has someone that can use computers as part of the magick. I would find hard to believe that the Alexandrian society of the Celestial Chorua or the Lacksmits Eutanatoi haven't computer saavi agents.<br /> <br /> The Digital Web has it's biggest Traditionalist pressence in the hands of the VA and the Etherites, but there are sites build by mages of every tradition, even if they're few in comparison.<br /> <br /> All of this it's documented in the book of Digital Web and the various Tradition books.<br /> <br /> The trick to know how a techno-saavi mage will operate it's to think holistically. Tradition magick isn't a degree, but a way of life, any Traditional mage that it's saavi with computers, and uses them as a way of life, can figure a way to use this trait in combination with his beliefs (belief can be very flexible).<br /> Those mages who have included technology in their arcane works (or viceversa), have no trouble mantaining a sophisticated library online, or programing games with esoterical messages and content. Also, even if a mage hasn't tech as a focus, that doesn't mean that he can't know enough of computers as to affect them with magick. For instance, an Akashick could meditate in order to use Mind to enhance his mundane hacking skills. A Shaman could summon a tech savvi spirit without being tech saavi herself.<br /> <br /> Less tech oriented mages can still use the web, creating divulgation pages mantaining libraries, and so on. They can't build a magical computer, but they can send a mail like any guy. They just ain't going to leave valuable information on computers if they haven't the assistance of a tech saavi mage to protect it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-12-2017, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T17:31:51-08:00","id":1030883,"title":"","content":"See? I realize this is canon. But personally, I don't like Technomancer traditionalists outside of the VA and Etherites. Because when you get right down to it, they CAN do everything with the old ways, and by virtue of being mages, they should WANT to do everything with the old ways.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T18:28:41-08:00","id":1030917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030587-how-the-traditions-incorporate-computers-and-the-internet?p=1030883#post1030883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See? I realize this is canon. But personally, I don't like Technomancer traditionalists outside of the VA and Etherites. Because when you get right down to it, they CAN do everything with the old ways, and by virtue of being mages, they should WANT to do everything with the old ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going with that logic, the Euthanatos wouldn't want to use guns because they should want to do things the old ways...<br /> <br /> Also, Just as there are Technomancing Mystics. There as also Mystic Etherites and Virtual Adepts.<br /> <br /> There might be an Etherite that is and archaeologist who studies ancient mystic artefacts and the way they affect the laws of the universe. They are a scientist, yes, but they don't build things or use tech, they tap the secrets of these ancient forgoten artefacts. (Note, these are not Wonder Artefacts, but just objects from a lost civilisation the Etherite is researching.)<br /> <br /> There might be a Virtual Adept who thinks Computers are an unnecessary step their fellow Adepts rely upon for tapping into the true Universal Source code. Hacking reality can be done much more efficiently if you read the coding language of the universe rather than rely on a computer to translate it for you. Their method of magic may be through doing certain things at the correct time, so that the correct values are in the correct place for really weird &quot;reality glitches&quot; to take place. Basically they see the world as a video game, and their erratic behaviour is like accessing cheat codes, or glitches to get what they want. No tech needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 01-12-2017, 09:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T18:54:48-08:00","id":1030935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030587-how-the-traditions-incorporate-computers-and-the-internet?p=1030883#post1030883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See? I realize this is canon. But personally, I don't like Technomancer traditionalists outside of the VA and Etherites. Because when you get right down to it, they CAN do everything with the old ways, and by virtue of being mages, they should WANT to do everything with the old ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really when it comes right down to it. Starting with just the (pardon the persopnal phrase here) &quot;mundanities of magick&quot;; you need some dragon's teeth for something? It's gonna be easier and quicker to use the interwebs to get in contact with other mages across the world and see who might have dragon's teeth and be willing to part with them or barter for them. You want to research ancient Hermetic symbols? You could go through all the tomes and texts at the local chantry, or you could network with other Hermetics.<br /> <br /> Once you start with using the internet for communication, sharing of secrets and bartering for hard-to-find goods, it's a reasonable next step to think &quot;huh, I should probably do something to make sure my magickal dealings across the ocean of information is more secure&quot;, and using magick to do that isn't unreasonable. And going from there having a selection, small or large, of &quot;technomagical Verbena rotes&quot; designed to help with using this powerful tool isn't unreasonable.<br /> <br /> After all, communing with covens across the globe through chalices of blood might be more fun, but you have a higher likelyhood of catching some paradox that way as opposed to just FaceTiming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T19:17:53-08:00","id":1030952,"title":"","content":"I find that, even if a Mystic isn't prepared to delve completely into technomancy, there's utility in being able to bend these newfangled devices to one's methods. Indeed, the ability to justify doing so only strengthens one's Paradigm, because it proves that even modern machines obey the Old Laws. Just, you know, in a different way.<br /> <br /> A Verbana that curses someone by giving them the Evil Eye through a Selfie. A Hermetic who speaks words of power through a phone line. A Dreamspeaker who carries a picture of a shrine dedicated to his ancestors as the wallpaper of his smart phone. A Chorister who sends a blessing via text message, with a ASCII picture of a cross.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T04:47:00-08:00","id":1031087,"title":"","content":"Symbols are a very traditional instrument, and a gun pointed at you at close range is a more universal act of intimidation than a bone rattled in your direction.<br /> <br /> I see no problem in using tech (you grew up with) in mystic ways.<br /> <br /> The Traditions are not stuck with old ways. You can play a space opera without even one classical technomancer among the players (or even among the NPCs)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T05:23:25-08:00","id":1031099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030587-how-the-traditions-incorporate-computers-and-the-internet?p=1030883#post1030883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See? I realize this is canon. But personally, I don't like Technomancer traditionalists outside of the VA and Etherites. Because when you get right down to it, they CAN do everything with the old ways, and by virtue of being mages, they should WANT to do everything with the old ways.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That is what the Technocracy says about the Traditions. They want to take away indoor plumbing, electricity etc. While in theory there are members of the traditions like that, the official line is a return to the situation that predates the Ascension War:Multiple Paradigms cooexisting but in a more harmonious nature. So the offical plan wouldn't be &quot;No more Iphones' but rather &quot;hey lets make a magical app that lets you talk to Ghosts!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T08:41:30-08:00","id":1031174,"title":"","content":"See, here's the thing though. The Old ways are just as viable as the new ways. They work. Just as well. The only difference is that the Technocracy has spent centuries trying to stamp out belief in other kinds of magic so that the things they build get ALL the belief juice.<br /> <br /> You want to network with other wizards? Build a crystal ball network with a mind 2/Correspondence 3-4 effect. Carry a magic mirror a la harry potter. There are so many ways to make this work it's unbelievable and all it requires is a little work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T09:17:27-08:00","id":1031195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030587-how-the-traditions-incorporate-computers-and-the-internet?p=1031174#post1031174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, here's the thing though. The Old ways are just as viable as the new ways. They work. Just as well. The only difference is that the Technocracy has spent centuries trying to stamp out belief in other kinds of magic so that the things they build get ALL the belief juice.<br /> <br /> You want to network with other wizards? Build a crystal ball network with a mind 2/Correspondence 3-4 effect. Carry a magic mirror a la harry potter. There are so many ways to make this work it's unbelievable and all it requires is a little work.</div> </div> </div> </div>What requires less work? Making a series of crystal balls which are connected via Correspondence, and then making use everyone carries them on their person. Dealing with any Paradox that comes from such communication;<br /> Or having their phone number?<br /> <br /> Yes, there will be Hermetics that have rejected all forms of Tech because &quot;The old ways are just as good&quot;. But to say every Hermetic should think this way is to share these Hermetic's arrogance. Curmudgeons are only one side of the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T09:28:59-08:00","id":1031204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030587-how-the-traditions-incorporate-computers-and-the-internet?p=1031174#post1031174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, here's the thing though. The Old ways are just as viable as the new ways. They work. Just as well.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Build a crystal ball network with a mind 2/Correspondence 3-4 effect. Carry a magic mirror a la harry potter. There are so many ways to make this work it's unbelievable and all it requires is a little work.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not &quot;just as well&quot; as sending a message. One requires access to the spheres involved, a crystal ball, and a prayer that you don't botch. The other requires a phone, access to a public library with computers (or, obviously, owning your own), or any other of the hundreds of ways you can gain ready access to the internet or just a simple telephone. There is a huge gulf there that is not &quot;works just as well&quot; or &quot;just as viable&quot;. Not in Mage, where Paradox is just as real as a burner phone you bought at a local convenience store (which, again, won't cause Paradox).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T09:34:06-08:00","id":1031214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030587-how-the-traditions-incorporate-computers-and-the-internet?p=1031204#post1031204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Paradox is just as real as a burner phone you bought at a local convenience store (which, again, won't cause Paradox).</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless it's the Samsung Note 7. That had a huge paradox backlash on it when it was released.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T09:38:54-08:00","id":1031216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030587-how-the-traditions-incorporate-computers-and-the-internet?p=1031214#post1031214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless it's the Samsung Note 7. That had a huge paradox backlash on it when it was released.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that is why the Technocracy slowly leaks new tech to the public. When some company, like Samsung, tries to release something that the Consensus isn't ready for, bad things happen. But, my petulant whiny side wants to point out &quot;I SAID BURNER PHONE, NOT SMARTPHONE!!!!!&quot; But I think I have that side well under control, so no need to mentio-<br /> <br /> ... Wait. Crap. Nevermind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T10:04:46-08:00","id":1031225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find that, even if a Mystic isn't prepared to delve completely into technomancy, there's utility in being able to bend these newfangled devices to one's methods. Indeed, the ability to justify doing so only strengthens one's Paradigm, because it proves that even modern machines obey the Old Laws. Just, you know, in a different way.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> This it's the way that many real life modern mystics think, and fictional mystics shouldn't be any different. Magick has to be relevant to the day to day life of mortals in order to be of interest to anyone. People search mystical help over mundane problems, and thus mages have to understand these problems to be of any use to their comunities (unless you live in the Umbra)<br /> <br /> Want to protect your e-mail of those nasty hackers that appear in the news?, well, you could study computer science and then create a form of magick that blends with this new ways (which will take years). Ask a favor from another that knows about these machines...<br /> Or you could see if the old utterance of protection that you use on your regular mail works on the new stuff...it may need some adjustements, but the divine law of the universe has to rule everything, even this new machines (and the best part it's that this mystic &quot;Ward against Hackers&quot; WILL work, to the dismay of the VA <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). And then you will be able to help your acolites that have this same problem in their mundane lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-13-2017, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T10:29:08-08:00","id":1031236,"title":"","content":"Even a small application of technology has the potential to greatly enhance Traditional magic, particularly rituals. Don't have time to properly draw an eighty one point star? Render it in a graphics program. Need to coordinate your ritual participants at their designated points across the country? Skype that shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T16:15:20-08:00","id":1031374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030587-how-the-traditions-incorporate-computers-and-the-internet?p=1031204#post1031204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is not &quot;just as well&quot; as sending a message. One requires access to the spheres involved, a crystal ball, and a prayer that you don't botch. The other requires a phone, access to a public library with computers (or, obviously, owning your own), or any other of the hundreds of ways you can gain ready access to the internet or just a simple telephone. There is a huge gulf there that is not &quot;works just as well&quot; or &quot;just as viable&quot;. Not in Mage, where Paradox is just as real as a burner phone you bought at a local convenience store (which, again, won't cause Paradox).</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'm sure being able to say some magic words and hurtle fireballs at someone would be mighty convenient for a technocrat. But they don't. Why? They know it's POSSIBLE. They know they COULD do it.<br /> <br /> They just think it's wrong.<br /> <br /> And in the end, buying a burner phone to coordinate your mystical whatever is basically ASKING for the Technocracy to know everything you do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T16:56:08-08:00","id":1031380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030587-how-the-traditions-incorporate-computers-and-the-internet?p=1031374#post1031374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I'm sure being able to say some magic words and hurtle fireballs at someone would be mighty convenient for a technocrat. But they don't. Why? They know it's POSSIBLE. They know they COULD do it.<br /> <br /> They just think it's wrong.<br /> <br /> And in the end, buying a burner phone to coordinate your mystical whatever is basically ASKING for the Technocracy to know everything you do.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of why you'd use a Burner phone. They are notoriously difficult to trace.<br /> <br /> Also code.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T17:44:07-08:00","id":1031392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030587-how-the-traditions-incorporate-computers-and-the-internet?p=1031374#post1031374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I'm sure being able to say some magic words and hurtle fireballs at someone would be mighty convenient for a technocrat. But they don't. Why? They know it's POSSIBLE. They know they COULD do it.<br /> <br /> They just think it's wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you're saying the Traditions think using modern technology is inherently wrong, something never stated in any book anywhere, then I don't see where you're going with that or how you defend it. Are you saying that the Traditions cannot adapt their rotes to use with technology because the Technocracy hates old school magick? Because that makes no sense, what with the SoE and VA being in the nine Traditions. Are you saying no Traditions would ever adopt technomancy rotes? The tradition books would argue otherwise.<br /> <br /> I'd also argue the Technocracy don't know it's possible for them to throw fireballs. They don't think what they do and what the Traditions do is the same thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030587-how-the-traditions-incorporate-computers-and-the-internet?p=1031374#post1031374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And in the end, buying a burner phone to coordinate your mystical whatever is basically ASKING for the Technocracy to know everything you do.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Technocracy is already spying on you to tell what, again, <b>burner phone</b> you just bought and have the resources available to crack into it and listen in on all your calls, then you're already on their radar. No amount of crystal ball communication is gonna help you or make a difference. But also, that's why (as I mentioned before) you'd probably see Traditionalists learning some basic tech-based rotes, or as someone else mentioned, adopting their non-tech based ones to use with technology.<br /> <br /> And again, it's still Paradox-free. and Paradox is something Tradition mages try and avoid as much as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T18:06:06-08:00","id":1031396,"title":"","content":"Code's can be circumvented with Mind. In essence, this is a battle of wizardry, and while mundane tools can help, communications is not one of those things. Communication is something you want as secure as humanly possible. You want to use the very best of what you can get to make sure there's no chance whatsoever of being intercepted. A sequence of mirrors with a consecrated stone at the top, that project a mind effect so that the user can talk to another user is both coincidental (As far as everyone else is concerned you're just talking to yourself while holding a mirror. weird but not &quot;Oh my god! MAgic!&quot;) Relatively simple to set up. And best of all nigh on impossible for the Technocrats to practically tap in on. Unlike mass produced technology which is, I might remind you, based entirely on technocratic designs.<br /> <br /> It's one thing to pick up a gun so you're not throwing around firebolts in the middle of battle and getting exploded by paradox. It's another thing entirely to communicate secret plans over <i>skype.</i><br /> <br /> For the street cabal? Who just got into magic like a week ago? Sure. But for an established Chantry...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T18:23:26-08:00","id":1031403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030587-how-the-traditions-incorporate-computers-and-the-internet?p=1031396#post1031396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the street cabal? Who just got into magic like a week ago? Sure. But for an established Chantry...</div> </div> </div> </div>For your established chantry, who doesn't want to walk around carrying mirrors down the street and talking into them... You've got Virtual Adepts who are more than capable of securing your phones. You've got tech-based factions within all or nearly all of the Traditions, likewise capable of utilizing rotes to scramble and unscramble calls. And best of all, all of this is well within the consensus and nobody looks at you funny for talking into a phone. Well, depending on what you say.<br /> <br /> You said the old ways are equal to the newfangled technoboogityboo. So far, you've only been able to show examples where they reach parity under very narrow conditions (not in transit, lots of prep time with rotes, everyone else using the same rotes as you, the phone being known to the Technocracy upon purchase, that phone not being secured by the same rotes to prevent magickal scrying you'd presumably use to protect the mirror-comms and under the hope no Paradox hits you). Nobody is saying there won't be hoary old archmages wandering around who curmudgeonly refuse to use the latest doodads, or Luddites among the Traditions (possibly quite a few) who refuse to wield the tools of the Technocracy. But saying their ways are equal is just not true.<br /> <br /> Also, depending on distance, your scrying mirror will need Correspondence as well as Mind. You'd only need Correspondence 2 to ward off scrying attempts from the phone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T19:09:53-08:00","id":1031415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">. Communication is something you want as secure as humanly possible. You want to use the very best of what you can get to make sure there's no chance whatsoever of being intercepted. A sequence of mirrors with a consecrated stone at the top, that project a mind effect so that the user can talk to another user is both coincidental (As far as everyone else is concerned you're just talking to yourself while holding a mirror. weird but not &quot;Oh my god! MAgic!&quot;) Relatively simple to set up. And best of all nigh on impossible for the Technocrats to practically tap in on. Unlike mass produced technology which is, I might remind you, based entirely on technocratic designs.<br /> <br /> It's one thing to pick up a gun so you're not throwing around firebolts in the middle of battle and getting exploded by paradox. It's another thing entirely to communicate secret plans over <i>skype.</i></div> </div> </div> </div><i>Well, you aren't going to communicate <u>secret</u> plans over Skype</i>, unless you have some serious mojo to keep them safe (which many established Traditionalists have, mind you), you are going to communicate normal, less secret, plans.<br /> Same goes for Technocrats. They're as paranoid if not more than the Traditions in this regard. I would imagine that the Technocracy would communicate important stuff using a very secure network, only hackeable trough magick.<br /> <br /> It's worth to note that Magick can be detected and traced in big areas (it's just Correspondence 3, Prime 1. NWO has big radars to detect supernatural activity, so it's not rare). Having this in mind, it may be better to avoid using magick in comunications, if it isn't strictly necessary. Use your best magick to communicate the plans to attack the local Construct, not to discuss occult Hermetic trivia with other (probably mortal) occultists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I'm sure being able to say some magic words and hurtle fireballs at someone would be mighty convenient for a technocrat. But they don't. Why? They know it's POSSIBLE. They know they COULD do it.<br /> <br /> They just think it's wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>And haven't you guessed already that this it's the difference between Technocrats and Traditionalists?<br /> <br /> Technocrats have a very restrictive view on magick (when they even deign themselves to recognize it as real). One World, One Reality, One Truth.<br /> <br /> In contrast, the Traditions defend a free view on magick. Sure, some Masters might frown, but they won't openly forbbid new-age technosorcery trends, even if they might discourage them. Each mage do as they Will in the Traditions, that's their philosopy. That's why they're so chaotic, and so diverse. It's their strength, and their weakness.<br /> <br /> Thats how things are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-13-2017, 10:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}